            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "health_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I removed `suspend`, `hibernate`, etc. here because I could not find evidence that those are expected to be \"irreversible\".  We don't actually use those on the BMC anyhow.  If you can find evidence, please update the commit with a link."
                },
                {
                    "file": "health_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zane Li",
                        "email": "zane.li.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Zane-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the feedback.\nAs a reference, in https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/v257.5/src/systemctl/systemctl-start-unit.c#L226, the logic shows which targets are considered to need \"replace-irreversibly\". For targets like suspend/hibernate which we won\u2019t use on BMC, removing them makes sense. Thanks for pointing this out."
                }
            ],
